-- Generated by tools/changelog/build.py; regenerate rather than edit.

local _, ns = ...

ns.MapChangelog = {
	{ version = "Unreleased", date = "", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon maps use the client's language|r: Forever's dungeon floors and wings now use the translated names and map artwork from the client's own game files, including Blackrock Spire and Dire Maul.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon and raid bosses use the client's language|r: Forever now includes contributor-authored boss translations for every supported locale, with English fallback where no translation is available. Season of Discovery-only encounters and duplicate combined encounters were removed from Gnomeregan and Sunken Temple; Blackfathom Deeps keeps its Vanilla Baron Aquanis and Lorgus Jett entries.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.2", date = "2026-11-08", heads = { [1] = "Improved", [2] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aPanning no longer hitches|r: the map set up to 300 textures' files in a single frame where a pan brought new ground into view, and each set is a load and an upload, so that frame showed as a hitch of about 35 ms. It sets 60 a frame now; the art still fades in, a few frames later.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map no longer stalls a moment after it opens|r: since 0.8.0 OpenMap keeps the map's art loaded while it's closed, then let go of it all in one frame a second into the opening, which the game unloaded at once (about a second's freeze). It now lets go of it a little at a time.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZooming in notch by notch is smooth again|r: since 0.8.1 the blur came back all at once each time the map stopped, one long frame the next wheel notch landed on. It now waits out a pause between notches and comes back a few zones a frame. Questie's mob paths are worked out once the map stops, not on every frame of a zoom.",
	{ version = "v0.8.9", date = "2026-11-14", heads = { [1] = "New", [4] = "Improved", [9] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aHide world markers in instances|r (the menu's On the map tab, and Options; off unless turned on): in dungeons, raids and battlegrounds, OpenMap's friends, guild, transport and all-zone quest markers step aside. With Dungeon maps off and another addon's dungeon map shown over the world (NeedRoll's), the world under it stops answering the mouse, and a right-click brings the world map back, at the dungeon's outdoor entrance (#232). By HonzoNebro.",
		"|cff6e2c0aPin options|r (OpenMap's options, Moving about and Sharing): - |cff6e2c0aFollow new pins|r: on by default, as before. Off, a pin you drop doesn't become the waypoint, so addons that route to it (Shortest Path Forever) are left alone; the pin's Follow still sets it. - |cff6e2c0aSend new pins to group|r: a pin you drop goes to your party or raid once its card is closed. - |cff6e2c0aAuto-add group's pins|r: pins your party or raid shares are added without asking. By diegodiaz1256.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA map of Blackmaw Hold|r, drawn by Santiago Reyes: all six of its floors, from Blackmaw Grove and the Festering Grotto down to the Depths of Forbidden Magic (the floor list at the top of the dungeon's map, or its arrows). (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aCity of Dalaran's map is Santiago Reyes's updated version, with the Underbelly|r, where the dungeon starts, as a second floor (#220). Opened inside the dungeon, the map shows the floor you're on.",
		"|cff6e2c0aShaper's Terrace's map is Santiago Reyes's final version, with the Prismatic Talus|r as a second floor.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe controller view's switch in the map's menu too|r: \"OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI (test)\" is under The map in OpenMap's menu as well as in Options (it was only in Esc > Options > AddOns, and a player took it for gone).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's quest icons in front|r: a \"!\" or \"?\" is no longer hidden under a flight master or a dungeon's icon; Questie's townsfolk stay under OpenMap's icons (#92).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA word about MapUtils|r: with MapUtils on, OpenMap says once in chat that the two both change the map's zoom, which made the map and Blizzard's quest areas jump while zooming (#160).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOne arrow for you, not two|r: where OpenMap draws your arrow itself (the map underneath can't place you), Blizzard's arrow now steps aside, so the two no longer show a little apart (#229).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuests from the tracker open on their details|r: the first click on a tracked quest opened the map on the quest list; it shows the quest's text now (#224).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map cooler on your graphics card|r: OpenMap's \"Map frame rate cap\" is now 60 by default (and set to 60 once for everyone): a still map was drawn as fast as the card could go (#233). Turn it off in Options if you'd rather.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFade while moving fades while you steer with the mouse|r: the hidden cursor's last place over the map held it solid, so it hardly ever faded (#69).",
		"|cff6e2c0aResizing the window keeps it where it is|r: it could jump to the screen's bottom left (#241).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNighthaven's flight master shows for druids only|r, as only druids can fly from it (#222).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe controller view takes the mouse too|r (OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI): the wheel zooms, a drag pans, and a click works as A (left) or X (right) (#234).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCity names in your language|r: Thunder Bluff's and Darnassus' name banners showed in English on other languages' clients; the zone map's own banner, in the client's language, is shown there now (#47).",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour quests' icons show in the controller view|r (Options' \"OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI\"): there were none, and no tooltips. Every quest in your log is now OpenMap's icon there, at any zoom, in every zone (with \"Quests from every zone\" off: the zone Blizzard's map is on); A tracks the quest and zooms to it. The \"!\" of quests you can start in that zone are there too, with the quest's name on the tooltip. The shaded quest areas aren't on it yet (#225). By k4m1.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZygor's map line stays thick on the stitched map|r: Zygor's route line (and its dots and waypoint icons) shrank to a thin grey line zoomed in and grew far too wide zoomed out, as Zygor sizes them for Blizzard's zoom range; they now stay the same size on screen at every zoom (#218). By rogeriocamorim.",
		"|cff6e2c0aGilneas shows on every language's client|r: on the Russian and Latin American Spanish clients Gilneas was a solid green square, as the game doesn't have its map's art in those languages (as with the dungeon and cave maps before v0.8.5). OpenMap now brings those tiles itself (#152). Found and tested by XaksFlaX. (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon level ranges|r: the dungeons' levels on the map are now the ones the game's Group Finder gives (each Scarlet Monastery and Dire Maul wing its own); they were an old level each, five levels wide, and some were far off: Razorfen Kraul showed 24-29 for a dungeon of 29-38 (#201). By ConfusionOrb221.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.8", date = "2026-11-13", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aParty and raid markers stay steady|r: one marker per member, moving smoothly. OpenMap's ring now follows Blizzard's own dot where the game places a member, instead of a second dot of its own that lagged behind it; elsewhere OpenMap's dot keeps its highlight and tooltip as it moves. The ring is now a thin gold edge (the wide one round a dark gap read as a target: #158, #170). By puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFriends on the map: your own faction only.|r Your place is only shared with, and shown from, players of your own faction: Battle.net friends on the other faction no longer see where you are, nor you them (a player's report: it let Horde and Alliance find each other for PvP).",
		"|cff6e2c0aFriends in another realm group show on the map|r: a friend on CAMWOW US1 and one on US2 (or EU4 and EU5) never saw each other with \"Share where you are\" on (#164, #167).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.7", date = "2026-11-12", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's icons show on the first map you open|r: with Questie 12.8, a map opened on a zone showed none of Questie's icons (their tooltips still came up) until you'd zoomed out to the continent once: icons Questie placed before the map was first opened stayed under its art (#194, #193, #195).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.6", date = "2026-11-12", heads = { [1] = "Improved", [2] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aIcons stay shown while zooming|r: \"Fade icons while zooming\" is now off for everyone, as zooming is smooth enough with them shown; turn it on again in the menu's On the map tab if you prefer it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's icons show again with Questie 12.8|r: Questie 12.8 brings its map icons a new way (its own module, with a new name), which OpenMap didn't know, so they were left off the map; and each icon Questie drew again sank under the map's art, so they faded away one by one. Older Questie versions work as before (#18). With bv101rj. Questie 12.8 hides its objective icons (mobs to kill, items to loot) until you turn them on: /questie, Icon Options, Objectives.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.5", date = "2026-11-12", heads = { [1] = "New", [4] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap's map with a controller|r (the game's Gamepad UI; a test, off until you turn it on in Options: \"OpenMap's map with the Gamepad UI (test)\"): the seamless map with the Gamepad UI on, where OpenMap leaves the world map to Blizzard. OpenMap draws its map over Blizzard's and leaves Blizzard's map as it is, so the controller's buttons keep working and closing the map with B is no longer blocked. The left stick moves the cursor (at the edge it pans), the right stick zooms about it, A zooms into a zone or presses the icon or button under the cursor, X zooms out or closes what's open, and pressing the left stick puts the waypoint there. On it: dungeons, boats, flight masters and their routes, your pins and the waypoint, your party, Questie's icons (with their tooltips), townsfolk and mob paths, other addons' icons (TomTom, gatherers), dungeon maps with their bosses, quests and loot, and the OpenMap menu with search, Find me, map pins, the quill (A puts the pen down, A lifts it) and Report a problem. Questie's icons no longer slow the map down there either. The D-pad's right opens the quest log, as on Blizzard's map. Off (the default): Blizzard's map with the Gamepad UI, as before. If you play with a controller, try it and tell us how it goes (#57). By FlyingPenguin98.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWoW Forever's newest dungeons on the map|r: Krol'dok Stronghold, Alcaz Prison, Blackmaw Hold and Shaper's Terrace have their entrance pins (#142), and they and The Drowned City list their bosses. By puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReopen the map on your zone|r (the menu's More tab, Reopen map: \"Center on your zone\"): the map opens on the whole zone you're in, in the middle, wherever you stand in it (#143).",
		"|cff6e2c0aRagefire Chasm shows with \"Only places you've found\"|r once you've found Orgrimmar: an entrance inside a city is found with the city, whose own map has nothing to explore (#113).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe Drowned City's map opens inside it|r: opening the map in one of WoW Forever's own dungeons that the game's tables didn't list yet (The Drowned City, Krol'dok Stronghold, Shaper's Terrace) showed the world map instead of its drawn map. With puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Darken unexplored areas\" keeps its soft edges up close|r: once the minimap's detail shows, the shade was hard-edged rectangles, and it changed as the minimap came in; it now has each unexplored area's own shape, as further out (#101, #129).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCave maps whole|r: Blizzard's cave maps showed only the parts their pale floors give away, cut off along a straight line near the page's foot (Maraudon's entrance, Wailing Caverns', Night Web's Hollow ...); the caves' own rooms now say where they are, as was meant (#141).",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo white diamonds at cave mouths|r: one of the game's own cave minimap pictures has a white block baked in over its tunnel's mouth, which showed up close at two caves in the Hinterlands (and one in Kalimdor); OpenMap now draws a mended copy (#114).",
		"|cff6e2c0a/openmap forgetflights|r forgets the flight paths OpenMap remembers as learned for the character, for one counted wrongly (route planners read the list); the next flight master's map learns the real ones again (#153).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.4", date = "2026-11-11", heads = { [1] = "New", [4] = "Improved", [5] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aBosses pinned on dungeon maps|r: a numbered pin where each boss is, on its floor, numbered as the Bosses tab lists them, with its name on the tooltip (click: its loot in NeedRoll). Placed from Blizzard's own dungeon journal for 153 bosses so far; \"Dungeon maps: bosses\" turns them off with the list (#90, #93).",
		"|cff6e2c0a/openmap bosses places the rest yourself|r: on a dungeon's map, click where the boss named in the bar is (right-click skips one, shift-click takes the last back). Your places show at once and are kept with your settings.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon maps from the minimap|r (Options, off): a dungeon's map built from the game's own minimap pictures of its rooms, a picture per floor, instead of its drawn map: The Hall of Thanes and Ruins of Lordaeron for now.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour party and raid get a gold-bordered dot|r on the stitched map, everywhere, so they can't be mistaken for a guild member's dot. Someone the game won't place is shown faintly in the middle of their zone, with \"Somewhere in\" on the tooltip. By KonigTX.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Your arrow\" off also hides the yellow location ping|r when the world map opens or changes zones. Turning it on again restores the normal arrow and ping; party markers stay visible (#78). By Luquatic.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Party and raid members\" off means off|r: Blizzard's own blips for your group are hidden too, not only OpenMap's dots (#77, found by Luquatic).",
		"|cff6e2c0aDragging the map no longer zooms into a zone or city|r: a drag that came back near where it started counted as a click and zoomed into what was under the cursor, Ironforge from parts of Dun Morogh most of all (#37, #64).",
		"|cff6e2c0aGuild markers clear when a guildmate joins your group|r: their shared-location dot or zone badge entry could stay when the guild roster and the party spelled the character's name differently. By puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Ctrl-click drops a pin\" off leaves Ctrl-click to other addons|r: with it off, a Ctrl-click zoomed the map and went no further, so Map Pin Enhanced's own Ctrl-click did nothing (#19).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOne map marker per friend or guildmate|r: different realm labels could make the same character count twice in a zone badge or show more than one shared-location dot (#104, #115). By puschie286.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo flight master at Powderfuse Port|r: the map showed one there, but there's none in the game yet; the port is reached by its boat, which stays on the map (#121, #132).",
		"|cff6e2c0aMap size in OpenMap's menu is greyed out with Move Any|r, as it is in Options: Move Any sizes the map then, and the menu's slider moved without changing anything (perhaps #136).",
	} },
}
